    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d101">

                <pb facs="0102" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg780"/>

                <head>Mr. Dayton to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 352.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-09-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 25, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch No. 391, as to the
                    proceedings of our minister resident at Salvador, in reference to French
                    interests there, and the despatch from him to you on that subject, were at once
                    communicated by me to the foreign office here. As it was evident that a copy of
                    Mr. Partridge’s despatch, stating what <pb facs="0103" n="781" xml:id="pg781"/>
                    he had done in relation to French interests in that country, should be on the
                    files of the foreign office here, I left the same temporarily with Mr. Drouyn de
                    l’Huys, at his request, that he might have it copied, if so disposed.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM L. DAYTON.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> H. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Seward</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
